# Security headers for asset-served responses, doc 15 §2.
#
# Most of TilePier's HTML is prerendered and served straight from the ASSETS
# binding, so the SvelteKit `handle` hook never runs for it — headers set only
# in hooks.server.ts would be missing from exactly the pages that matter.
# Caught by the e2e header assertion, which found `/` coming back bare.
#
# The main Content-Security-Policy is deliberately NOT here. SvelteKit emits it
# itself (svelte.config.js `kit.csp`, hash mode) because it has to include a
# hash for its own inline hydration script, and that changes every build — a
# static file cannot carry it. A second, fuller CSP here would be enforced
# alongside SvelteKit's, and since it would lack the hash it would block
# hydration all over again.
#
# The one directive below is the exception: `frame-ancestors` is ignored in a
# <meta> CSP by specification, so SvelteKit drops it from the tag it emits and
# it has to arrive as a header. A policy containing only `frame-ancestors` is
# safe to stack — browsers enforce each policy independently, and this one
# restricts nothing else.
#
# hooks.server.ts keeps a copy of these for dynamically rendered responses.
# Change both together; the e2e suite asserts the result on a real deploy.
#
# The adapter appends its own immutable-asset block below at build time —
# leave the AUTOGENERATED markers alone.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
